# What `git archive` leaves out of the published source tarball.
#
# This file affects archives only. Nothing here is removed from the repository
# or from a clone — `extra/` stays tracked, because it is operator reference
# material. See docs/design/packaging.md §6.4.
#
# Two properties to know before trusting it:
#
#   * Attributes are read from the tree being archived, so this is NOT
#     retroactive. `git archive v0.3.0` still carries everything, because that
#     tag's tree has no .gitattributes. Only tags cut after this commit are
#     covered, which matters because §3 tells recipes to build from a tag.
#   * It binds `git archive` and nothing else. A tarball rolled with `tar czf`
#     over a working tree ignores every line here, which is why §4 pins the
#     release tarball to `git archive`.
#
# Verify rather than assume — the failure is silent, with no error and no diff:
#
#   git archive HEAD --format=tar | tar -t | grep -v '/$'
#
# `grep -v '/$'` is not optional: `tar -t` lists directory entries too, and
# counting them is how an earlier draft of docs/design/packaging.md came to
# say `extra/` was ten files when it is seven. To check one rule rather than
# read the whole list, add `| grep '^extra/'` — it must print nothing.
#
# (Before this file is committed, add --worktree-attributes, or git reads the
# attributes from HEAD's tree and appears to ignore your edit.)

# Third-party xtables-addons source (GPL-2) plus ufw reference snippets.
# Bundled upstream source inside a release tarball is refused by Debian and
# Fedora packaging policy, and this project's root LICENSE is MIT. We depend
# on xtables-addons; we do not ship a second copy of it.
extra/ export-ignore

# Development history. A closed work log, a plan for work not done, and
# operating instructions for an AI assistant working in this repository —
# none of which a downstream packager can act on. 227,912 bytes, 18% of the
# tarball. All four stay tracked; `git log` and the release notes are the
# right place to read history from.
/DONE.md          export-ignore
/DONE_tldr.md     export-ignore
/TODO.md          export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md        export-ignore

